# Source: https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/332
# Symptom: BED12 line with a 13th extra column causes fastaFromBed -split to
#   treat the record as BED6 instead of BED12, returning the full feature span
#   rather than just the splice-block sequences.  The extra column shifts the
#   block-fields detection heuristic.  Valid BED+ but triggers tool defect.
# The file is structurally valid BED12+1; the pathology is tool-side, but
#   validators should flag "extra columns beyond BED12 may confuse parsers".
